      "value": "@{5c096c483ce7d43ae0f1177e|full_name}: At this point I'm pretty sure this is a case of you distorting the truth. He likely got banned because the avatars *were* in fact public cancer, because of his behavior, or because he was using alternate avatars at the same time that WERE cancer.\n\nIf the avatar itself was public use and he got banned for it, you likely would have gotten banned as well. That should say enough about what you are considered to be by the public eye. This is further extended by the amount of screen shaders and extreme particle effects you release on VRCMods alone. \n\nSlapping on a tag to allow CLEARLY obnoxious, annoying, cancerous and generally TOS-breaking effects and sounds on an avatar should not be considered. Keep that stuff to a private instance out of anybody's way. Just like you would with R-18 avatars.\n\nBeing a creator, I'm all for giving rights and customizability to all content creators. But this... This is not the way to go about it. \nThis only supports you, your friends, and people very similar to you. Not content creators as a whole.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
