      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Giving people the freedom to create content is important. However, making (and distributing) malicious avatars isn't OK. If you choose to make things designed to be unpleasant, you're likely to run into issues with players as well as moderation.\n\nAdditionally, no matter what content you choose to upload to VRChat, you must abide by the Community Guidelines and Terms of Service. Roughly speaking, the Community Guidelines prohibits content that can be used to harass or \"troll\" other users. No matter the original intent or use case of the content in question, if an avatar (for example) is considered harassing, malicious, or abusive, it can and will be removed from the service at the discretion of the VRChat Moderation team.\n\nWe ask that you use common sense in determining what could be used in this manner. The Safety System is meant as a mitigation for users abusing avatar systems, and is not an excuse for avatar creators to create abuse-able setups or systems.\n\nAs a final addendum, no matter the checkboxes available in the SDK, content must never violate the Community Guidelines or Terms of Service.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
